A note about the built plugin, which this license does not change:

The sources in this repository are MIT, and anybody may take them on those terms.
The plugin that is built from them is a different matter. It inherits `BasePlugin<T>`
and links `Jellyfin.Controller` and `Jellyfin.Model`, which Jellyfin publishes under
`GPL-3.0-only`. The compiled `Jellyfin.Plugin.Sso.dll`, and the release zip that
carries it, are therefore distributed under the GNU General Public License, version 3
— the terms of the libraries they are built against. MIT grants everything the GPL
needs granted, so the two sit together without conflict; the GPL is simply the stricter
of the two, and it is the one that travels with the binary.

In short: copy the code under MIT, pass the plugin on under GPLv3.
